# Clean Code Principles (Index)

Clean code guidance is split into focused rule files. Request the one that matches your task:

| Topic | File | When to Use |
|-------|------|-------------|
| **Naming and intent** | `patterns/clean-code-naming.mdc` | Naming conventions, vocabulary, abbreviations, negated booleans |
| **Function structure** | `patterns/clean-code-functions.mdc` | Method parameters, guard clauses, abstraction levels, cognitive load |
| **Design principles** | `patterns/clean-code-design.mdc` | Side effects, immutability, Law of Demeter, composition, dependencies |
| **Code hygiene** | `patterns/clean-code-hygiene.mdc` | Dead code, magic numbers, comments, fail fast, Rule of Three |

**See also:** `architecture.mdc`, `testing.mdc`
